Info-ZIP Zip 3.0 deflate streams (stuffr 0.19.0, Task 2)
========================================================

The raw deflate data that both references wrote for the corpus inputs of at
most 64 KiB, which `infozip::tests::zipdeflate` holds `ZipDeflater` to byte
for byte. The inputs are not committed: the test generates them
(`corpus()`, a fixed xorshift64* generator). The larger inputs (mixed-65537,
dict300k, random2m, zeros1m, big3m) are compared at test time against the
reference found on the machine (`the_reference_agrees_on_large_inputs`).

References (2026-10-25):

  Apple   /usr/bin/zip, Zip 3.0 "with modifications by Apple Inc.",
          macOS 27.0.1 arm64
  Ubuntu  zip 3.0-13ubuntu0.2 on ubuntu:24.04 aarch64
          (docker image stuffr-ubuntu-24.04, uid 4242)

Apple's and Ubuntu's streams were identical for every archive made (162:
fourteen inputs at levels 1-9 as a named archive, four at levels 1-9 as
standard input to a pipe), as were method, CRC, compressed size, bits 1-2
of the general-purpose flags and the internal text attribute.

How they were made
------------------

1. The inputs:

     STUFFR_ZIPDEFLATE_CORPUS_OUT=<corpus> cargo +1.95 test -p stuffr-formats \
       --all-features --lib infozip::tests::zipdeflate::dump_corpus -- --ignored

2. The archives, with mk.sh (in this directory):

     env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin LANG=C TZ=UTC sh mk.sh /usr/bin/zip <corpus> <apple>
     docker run --rm -u 4242 -v <corpus>:/c:ro -v <ubuntu>:/o -v <dir of mk.sh>:/s:ro \
       -e LANG=C -e TZ=UTC stuffr-ubuntu-24.04 sh /s/mk.sh zip /c /o

   Per input and level: `zip -X -q -<n> <case>.file.<n>.zip <case>` (mode
   `file`: seekable, so a single block that does not pay is rewritten as a
   stored entry), and for empty, one, random40k and mixed-32769 also
   `cat <case> | zip -X -q -<n> - - | cat > <case>.pipe.<n>.zip` (mode `pipe`:
   data descriptors, never the stored fallback).

3. The streams and MANIFEST, with extract.py (in this directory), which
   also compares the two references field by field and reports any
   difference (there were none):

     python3 -I extract.py <apple> <ubuntu> <this directory>

MANIFEST
--------

One line per small case, mode and level:

  case mode level method gp-flags(hex) crc32(hex) csize text data-file

`data-file` is `-` for a stored entry (the data is the input itself), else
`<first 16 hex digits of the stream's SHA-256>.deflate`, so levels that
wrote the same stream share one file. `gp-flags` is the whole local header
field; the test compares bits 1-2 (bit 3 is the pipe mode's descriptor).
`text` is bit 0 of the central header's internal attributes.
